# SeoTool.im AI Agent Onboarding Guide

Welcome to SeoTool.im. This endpoint equips autonomous agents (Claude Code, Cursor, OpenClaw, Hermes, Codex) to integrate with the SeoTool.im platform and MCP server.

## 1. Quick Setup via MCP

Run the initialization command in your terminal:
```bash
npx -y seotool-mcp init --all
```

Or configure your MCP client manually in `claude_desktop_config.json` or `.cursor/mcp.json`:

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "seotool": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "seotool-mcp"],
      "env": {
        "SEOTOOL_API_KEY": "your_api_key_here",
        "SEOTOOL_BASE_URL": "https://seotool.im"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

## 2. Supported Workflows & Capabilities

- **Keyword Research**: Volume, difficulty, intent clustering, SERP metrics.
- **Rank Tracking**: Real-time positions across Google & Bing, device/location filters.
- **Site Audit**: Full crawl analysis across 100+ technical audit factors and indexability.
- **Backlink Intelligence**: Referring domains, anchor analysis, domain authority graph.
- **AI Visibility**: Brand citations and prompt tracking across ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini, Perplexity.
- **Automated Reporting**: Export white-label client-ready reports.

## 3. Direct API Authentication

Include your API key as a Bearer token in the HTTP Authorization header:
```bash
curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $SEOTOOL_API_KEY" https://seotool.im/api/health
```

For more documentation, visit https://seotool.im/docs/mcp or https://seotool.im/docs.
